# Real bank statements — NEVER commit these.
#
# They carry the account holder's real name and home address, the account IBAN,
# a dozen counterparty IBANs, balances, and a full spending history. The remote
# is a public GitHub URL, so a committed statement is a permanent public
# disclosure that no later commit can take back. No redacted copy is committed
# either: the user chose local reference over committed fixtures.
#
# The statements live in ~/Documents/Banking, OUTSIDE this working tree, and
# backend/finance/tests/integration/test_real_statement_reconciliation.py reads
# them from LIFEOS_STATEMENTS_DIR (default ~/Documents/Banking). The rules below
# are the second line of defence, for the copy someone eventually drags in.
#
# They match on filename shape rather than on `*.pdf`, because three of the four
# Rabobank files carry NO extension at all — the reconciliation tests find them
# by PDF magic bytes for the same reason, and a rule that only matched `*.pdf`
# would let the most identifiable of them straight through.
**/Banking/
**/Rabo/
**/Rev/
**/Amex/
Rabo Banking details
Rabo Banking details*
rabobank-*.pdf
rabobank-20??-??*
account-statement_*.pdf
account-statement_*
# Amex names a file for the day it was generated: 2026-06-23.pdf.
20??-??-??.pdf
